# The acceptance image is built with the repository root as its context (`scripts/acceptance.sh`,
# `docker/Dockerfile`), and the context is copied to the daemon before the first instruction runs.
# `target/` is tens of gigabytes of build artifacts the image rebuilds in its own cache mount, and
# on a machine whose temporary space is quota-bound, sending it is what filled the quota and
# killed the shell mid-session. Nothing below is an input to the build.
target/
.git/
